create user & passwd for the same ---->
user, passwd
admin, admin
web_user, web_user
db_user, db_user

---------------------------------

Generate Private & Public Keys ---->
ssh-keygen -f ~/.ssh/admin
ssh-keygen -f ~/.ssh/web_user
ssh-keygen -f ~/.ssh/db_user

---------------------------------

Copy keys from local to target hosts ---->
ssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/admin admin@$WEB1_IP
ssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/web_user web_user@$WEB1_IP

ssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/admin admin@$DB1_IP
ssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/db_user db_user@$DB1_IP

NOTE: Don't create any passphrase

---------------------------------

Login to target host to validate the keys working fine or not ------->


ssh -i ~/.ssh/admin admin@$WEB1_IP
ssh -i ~/.ssh/web_user web_user@$WEB1_IP

ssh -i ~/.ssh/admin admin@$DB1_IP
ssh -i ~/.ssh/db_user db_user@$DB1_IP


OR

ansible -i ./inventory all -m ping

---------------------------------

Adhoc commands:

ansible localhost -m archive -a 'path=./tmp_output dest=./tmp_out.tar.gz'

ansible -i ./inventory.yaml localhost -m unarchive -a 'src=./tmp_out.tar.gz dest=./dummy_unarchive_files'

